; the web's first engine, and its browser. The libraries, mosaic_layout
; and mosaic_engine, are how a page was laid out before CSS's box model: each element's
; look fixed by the browser (Mosaic_looks: Mosaic's table), blocks
; stacked and words set on lines in one pass (Mosaic_layout), drawn
; (Mosaic_draw), the three put together as an engine the browser's
; page pipeline takes (Mosaic_page). With ~extensions, what Netscape
; added -- <font>, <center>, floats, tables, bgcolor -- and with ~css
; the first style sheets, CSS1's properties over the looks: the same
; engine serves tools/netscape and tools/firefox. It was the browser's
; own until Box_layout replaced it; it is here to be read first.
; the looks and the layout: pure, no shapes and no fonts (the caller
; gives the widths), so their tests run on strings
(library
 (name mosaic_layout)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules Mosaic_looks Mosaic_layout)
 (libraries mini_dom lang_html lang_css browser_layout))

; the drawing, and the three as an engine
(library
 (name mosaic_engine)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules Mosaic_draw Mosaic_page)
 (libraries
   elm_playground ; the shapes it draws
   mini_dom lang_html lang_css browser_layout browser_display browser_www
   mosaic_layout
   appkit_typeset)) ; Linebreak, for wrap=pretty
